<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Aalen</h1><p class="st-meta">1360 CE – 1802 CE (approx.) · capital Aalen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small imperial city at the edge of the Swabian Jura, built beside the largest Roman cavalry fort on the Raetian limes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Aalen stands beside the largest Roman cavalry fort north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, built in the 2nd century on the Raetian limes. The medieval town was founded around 1240 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>. After a period pledged to the counts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-oettingen">Oettingen</a>, it was recognised as a free imperial city by Charles IV in 1360.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>One of the smallest imperial cities, Aalen was governed by a council and lived from crafts, farming, trade and iron ore mined nearby. It adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in 1575 and belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-circle">Swabian Circle</a>. A great fire in 1634, during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, destroyed much of the town.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1802 and 1803 Aalen was annexed by Württemberg, becoming part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wurttemberg">Kingdom of Württemberg</a> in 1806. Today it is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limes-museum-aalen">Limes Museum</a> stands on the site of the Roman fort.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1360 CE – 1802 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.77%;width:8.80%"></s